<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements of Vitrine Studio.app and the bundled `vitrine` CLI
  (Developer ID distribution, hardened runtime; ADR 0026).

  The app is NOT sandboxed: projects are arbitrary folders, the CLI and the
  GUI share them, the MCP proxy starts the GUI, and "Install command line
  tool" writes a symlink. Without com.apple.security.app-sandbox the sandbox
  entitlements (network.client, files.user-selected.read-write) have no
  effect, so none are listed:
  - network (store upload, gallery, updater, MCP on 127.0.0.1): allowed
    for non-sandboxed apps;
  - files: full user access like any non-sandboxed app (TCC still asks
    for protected folders such as Desktop/Documents);
  - keychain (`keyring`, generic passwords of service app.vitrinestudio):
    no entitlement needed outside the sandbox; items are bound to the code
    signature, so the first start of a newly signed build may ask once.
  Hardened-runtime exceptions: none. WKWebView runs JavaScript in Apple's
  own WebContent process, so allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
  are not needed; no plug-ins or unsigned libraries are loaded.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
